Third-party code

This repository does not include code of the predictors it compares. Each is cloned from its
repository at the commit used in the study, by the script that runs it:

  Predictor            Repository                                        Commit    License   Used by
  LM-OGlcNAc-Site      github.com/KCLabMTU/LM-OGlcNAc-Site               ff032df   none      analysis/06, scripts/lm_oglcnac_site_external
  O-GlcNAcPRED-DL      github.com/hufengzhu/O-GlcNAcPRED-DL-master       2e953b3   MIT       analysis/07
  RNN-[600,75]         github.com/PedroSeber/O-GlcNAcylation_Prediction  8d97344   MIT       analysis/08
  RNN-225              github.com/PedroSeber/O-GlcNAcylation_Prediction  b5629d5   MIT       analysis/08
  Stack-OglyPred-PLM   github.com/PakhrinLab/Stack-OglyPred-PLM          f9934d2   none      analysis/10, scripts/stack_oglypred_plm_long_proteins
  Arcanjo et al. 2025  github.com/LBS-UFMG/OGlcNAc                       c1d6d35   (our laboratory)  analysis/11

O-GlcNAcPRED-DL: analysis/07 changes some lines of the cloned files at run time (each change tagged
[modified] / [removed] in the files it writes). RNN-225 and RNN-[600,75]: run unchanged.

LM-OGlcNAc-Site and Stack-OglyPred-PLM have no license, so the scripts that run their code with our
changes are kept here as templates (*.template.py), in which every line taken from those repositories
is a reference to its file and line. third_party/assemble.py clones both repositories at the commits
above and writes the runnable scripts, checked to be identical to the scripts that were run.

YinOYang 1.2 (DTU Health Tech): analysis/09 prepares submission files for its web server; the
submissions failed, so it was not compared. No code is used.
